## Domain 2: Output Evaluation and Validation (21%)

### Question 2.1 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude summarizes an uploaded 40-page vendor contract and states "termination requires 90
days' notice." The manager will act on this next week. What is the best validation step?

**A.** Ask Claude to quote the supporting clause, and accept the figure if it does.

**B.** Find the termination clause in the contract itself and confirm the figure.

**C.** Re-run the summary in a fresh chat and confirm the same figure comes out.

**D.** Send the whole summary to legal counsel for review before relying on it.

### Question 2.2 · Expert · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude's research-mode competitor analysis includes citations. Spot-checking, the associate
finds one linked source supports a different market-share figure than the one stated. What
does this indicate, and what should happen?

**A.** The source is outdated; replace it with a more recent source for that figure.

**B.** The figure is a typo; correct it to match the number shown in the linked source.

**C.** A claim misstates its citation; check every cited figure against its source before
      use.

**D.** Research mode is unreliable here; redo the analysis in a standard chat instead.

### Question 2.3 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude drafts performance-review summaries for twelve staff from manager notes. Summaries
for the two part-time staff stress "availability" and "commitment," though their notes never
mention either. What is the right response?

**A.** Treat it as introduced bias: check each summary against its notes and remove the
      framing.

**B.** Add a neutral-language instruction to the prompt and regenerate all twelve summaries.

**C.** Ask Claude to review the summaries for bias and apply the changes it recommends.

**D.** Send all twelve summaries to HR for a bias review before any are finalized.

### Question 2.4 · Expert · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude drafts an internal FAQ answer on submitting expense claims, based solely on the
expense policy the associate uploaded. The associate wrote that policy and owns it. What
review does the answer need before publishing?

**A.** A legal review, since any policy-related content needs legal sign-off.

**B.** A second colleague's review, since authors miss errors in their own material.

**C.** A check by Claude against the uploaded policy, then publish if it confirms.

**D.** A check by the associate against the uploaded policy, then publish.

### Question 2.5 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude extracts action items from a 90-minute meeting transcript. Before circulating the
list, the associate wants to confirm no action item was missed. What is the most reliable
check?

**A.** Ask Claude to re-read the transcript and confirm that the list is complete.

**B.** Scan the transcript for commitments ("I'll…", "by Friday") and match each to the
      list.

**C.** Circulate the list and ask attendees to reply if anything is missing.

**D.** Compare the number of items against the number of agenda topics discussed.

### Question 2.6 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude has analyzed 300 survey responses. The finance team needs to filter the results by
region and re-sort them themselves in their own tools. Which output format fits?

**A.** An artifact report with a section per region and embedded charts.

**B.** An inline summary with each region's key findings as bullet points.

**C.** A table of responses with theme and region columns, exportable as CSV.

**D.** A slide-style artifact ranking the top themes for each region.

### Question 2.7 · Expert · Multiple choice · select ONE

An accurate, technical Claude analysis is going to the board. The board chair has asked that
the underlying analysis stay exactly as produced, for audit purposes. What is the best
adaptation?

**A.** Add a plain-language executive summary on top, leaving the technical body unchanged.

**B.** Rewrite the whole analysis in plain language, trimming the technical detail.

**C.** Ask Claude to simplify the wording throughout while preserving every figure.

**D.** Replace the technical body with charts and a short narrative for each finding.

### Question 2.8 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

Claude produces two job-posting drafts. The hiring manager prefers the tone of draft 1;
draft 2 lists every qualification in the approved requisition, draft 1 misses two. What
should the associate do?

**A.** Use draft 1, since the hiring manager owns the role and prefers its tone.

**B.** Use draft 2, since completeness matters more than tone in a job posting.

**C.** Ask Claude which draft better fits the role, and use the one it picks.

**D.** Check both against the requisition, then use draft 1's tone with every requirement.

### Question 2.9 · Expert · Multiple choice · select ONE

With no files, connectors or prior discussion of the topic, an associate asks Claude what
the CFO said at yesterday's internal all-hands. Claude returns a plausible summary. What
should the associate conclude?

**A.** Claude likely drew on public filings; confirm the summary against the latest one.

**B.** Claude had no access to the meeting; the summary is invented and should be discarded.

**C.** Claude may have drawn on memory from earlier chats; check what memory contains.

**D.** Claude inferred likely remarks from recent news; treat it as an approximation.

### Question 2.10 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

An associate researched a topic across several chats; some early findings were later
superseded. Colleagues need the findings next month. What should be shared?

**A.** An export of all the chats, so colleagues have the complete record.

**B.** A Claude summary of each chat, sent together as one bundle.

**C.** One document of the current, verified findings, with superseded ones removed.

**D.** The final answer from the latest chat, saved as an artifact and shared.

### Question 2.11 · Advanced · Multiple choice · select ONE

A Claude-drafted white paper cites "Smith et al. (2023), Journal of Retail Studies." The
associate cannot find the paper in any search. What is the right action?

**A.** Treat it as a likely fabricated citation; remove it or use a source you have
      verified.

**B.** Ask Claude for the paper's DOI and URL so the associate can locate it.

**C.** Keep it marked "citation pending" and verify it before the final release.

**D.** Rephrase the claim as general knowledge so it no longer needs a citation.

### Question 2.12 · Advanced · Multiple response · select TWO

A team wants fewer errors in Claude-drafted customer emails that quote order details and
sometimes offer remedies. Which TWO validation practices add the most? (Select TWO.)

**A.** Ask Claude to double-check order numbers before finishing each email

**B.** Compare quoted order numbers, dates and amounts against the order system before
      sending

**C.** Have Claude rate its confidence and send automatically when it rates above 90%

**D.** Generate each email twice and send only when both versions agree

**E.** Have a person review any email that commits to a refund or exception

### Question 2.13 · Advanced · Multiple response · select TWO

Claude summarizes a 60-page regulator consultation; the compliance team will use the summary
to decide whether and when to respond. Which TWO checks matter most before circulating?
(Select TWO.)

**A.** Confirm the summary fits the one-page limit the team requested

**B.** Ask Claude to list anything it was uncertain about while summarizing

**C.** Check each consultation question or section is covered or deliberately omitted

**D.** Rewrite the summary in plain language for non-specialist readers

**E.** Verify the response deadline and stated obligations against the original text

